        // Order: -L first (before RNG), then -f (RNG), then -N/-1/-2? But -1/-2 are based on input idx, not filtered idx? For -1/-2 with -f, we saw -f first then -1 (since f gave s0,s2,s4,s5 then -1 kept s0,s2,s4). That suggests -1 filtering after sampling, based on original idx (not sampled idx). Good.
        // For -L before -f, idx for -1/-2 should be original idx or filtered? Unclear. For simplicity, implement order: -L (min len) -> -f (sampling with RNG per passing -L) -> -N/-1/-2 (filtering sampled).
        // But -1/-2 based on original idx or sampled idx? For f+1 case, f gave s0,s2,s4,s5 (original indices 0,2,4,5), then -1 keeps even original indices (0,2,4) => s0,s2,s4 (drops s5 odd). Good - based on original idx.
